-- title:
--   The unit conversion cone equals three linear half-spaces
-- statement:
--   Let $(R,P,S)\in\mathbb R^3$ denote net public communication, private communication, and secret-key rates. The cone generated by secret-key distribution $(0,-1,1)$, the one-time pad $(-1,1,-1)$, and private-to-public transmission $(1,-1,0)$ has the exact description
--   $$
--   \{\alpha(0,-1,1)+\beta(-1,1,-1)+\gamma(1,-1,0):\alpha,\beta,\gamma\ge0\}
--   =\{(R,P,S):R+P\le0,\ R+P+S\le0,\ P+S\le0\}.
--   $$
--   This is the algebraic achievable cone of these three protocols; it does not assert a converse for all conceivable noiseless protocols.
-- source:
--   Public and private resource trade-offs for a quantum channel, arXiv:1005.3818v3, PDF p. 6, Section 4, eq. (9)

import Definitions.Def_QAlgorithms_Papers_Independent_Claimed50_P24

noncomputable section

